/**
 * Finds the optimal position within a given text segment to wrap a line,
 * respecting a maximum line width. The method prioritizes explicit line breaks
 * (newline, tab), then natural word breaks (whitespace), and finally
 * resorts to chopping a word if no other break points are found within the
 * specified width.
 *
 * The method considers the `width` as the maximum number of characters
 * allowed for the current line segment starting from `startPos`.
 *
 * @param text The complete string to be wrapped. Must not be null.
 * @param width The maximum desired length of the line segment. Must be a positive integer.
 * @param startPos The starting index in the `text` from which to begin searching for a wrap point.
 *                 Must be a non-negative integer and less than or equal to `text.length()`.
 * @return The index in the `text` where the current line should end, or where the next line should begin.
 *         <ul>
 *             <li>If an explicit newline ('\n') or tab ('\t') character is found within the `width` limit,
 *                 it returns the index immediately following that character (i.e., `pos + 1`).</li>
 *             <li>If a whitespace character (including space, newline, carriage return, tab, etc.,
 *                 as defined by {@link Character#isWhitespace(char)}) is found before the `width` limit,
 *                 it returns the index of that whitespace character, indicating a word break.</li>
 *             <li>If no suitable break point (explicit or whitespace) is found within the `width` limit,
 *                 and the text extends beyond `width`, it will search for the first whitespace character
 *                 *after* the `width` limit and return its index. This effectively "chops" the word.</li>
 *             <li>Returns -1 if:
 *                 <ul>
 *                     <li>The `startPos` is at or beyond the end of the `text`.</li>
 *                     <li>The remaining text from `startPos` to the end of the string is shorter than or equal to `width`.</li>
 *                     <li>No suitable wrap point is found, and the entire remaining segment from `startPos`
 *                         to `text.length()` is considered a single unbreakable unit that should extend
 *                         beyond the `width` (e.g., a very long word without spaces).</li>
 *                 </ul>
 *             </li>
 *         </ul>
 * @throws NullPointerException if `text` is null.
 * @throws IllegalArgumentException if `width` is not positive.
 * @throws IndexOutOfBoundsException if `startPos` is negative or greater than `text.length()`.
 */
