 * <p>The method ensures that valid Unicode surrogate pairs are generated if
 * characters within the surrogate range (U+D800 to U+DFFF) are chosen. If a single
 * high or low surrogate is randomly selected, a corresponding random low or high
 * surrogate is generated to form a complete pair, consuming two character positions
 * from the {@code count}. This prevents the generation of malformed Unicode strings.
 * If there isn't enough remaining {@code count} to form a pair, the single surrogate
 * is skipped.</p>
 *
 * @param count   the desired length of the random string to create. Must be non-negative.
 * @param start   the starting Unicode code point (inclusive) for character generation
