/**
 * Translates a numeric HTML/XML entity (e.g., {@code &#123;} or {@code &#x7B;}) at the specified index
 * within the input {@code CharSequence} and writes the corresponding Unicode character to the
 * provided {@code Writer}.
 *
 * <p>This method specifically handles decimal numeric entities (e.g., {@code &#123;}) and
 * hexadecimal numeric entities (e.g., {@code &#x7B;} or {@code &#X7B;}).
 * The entity must start with {@code "&#"} and end with a semicolon {@code ";"}.
 * For hexadecimal entities, an 'x' or 'X' must immediately follow the {@code "&#"}.</p>
 *
 * <p>If a valid numeric entity is found and successfully translated, the method writes the
 * corresponding character(s) to the {@code Writer} and returns the total number of characters
 * consumed from the input {@code CharSequence} for that entity (including {@code "&#"},
 * the numeric value, optional 'x', and {@code ";"}).</p>
 *
 * <p>If the sequence at the given index does not represent a valid numeric entity,
 * or if the entity is malformed (e.g., missing semicolon, invalid characters in the numeric part,
 * or an empty numeric value), or if the parsed numeric value is not a valid Unicode code point,
 * the method returns {@code 0}, indicating that no translation occurred and no characters were consumed.</p>
 *
 * @param input The {@code CharSequence} to be translated. Must not be {@code null}.
 * @param index The starting index in the {@code CharSequence} to begin translation.
 *              Must be a valid index within the {@code input} sequence.
 * @param out   The {@code Writer} to which the translated character(s) will be written. Must not be {@code null}.
 * @return The number of characters consumed from the input {@code CharSequence} if a numeric entity
 *         was successfully translated; otherwise, {@code 0}.
 * @throws IOException If an I/O error occurs while writing to the {@code Writer}.
 * @throws NullPointerException If {@code input} or {@code out} is {@code null}.
 */
