/**
 * Translates a portion of a {@code CharSequence} by performing a greedy longest-match lookup
 * against a predefined map of character sequences.
 * This method attempts to find the longest possible match from the {@code lookupMap}
 * starting at the given {@code index} in the {@code input} sequence.
 * If a match is found, the corresponding translated {@code CharSequence} is written
 * to the provided {@code Writer}, and the number of characters consumed from the input
 * (i.e., the length of the matched key) is returned.
 * If no match is found for any length within the {@code shortest} and {@code longest}
 * bounds of the lookup keys, no characters are written, and {@code 0} is returned.
 *
 * @param input The {@code CharSequence} to be translated. Must not be {@code null}.
 * @param index The starting index in the {@code input} {@code CharSequence} from which to begin translation.
